    "6:_": "Seif 6 forbidden etc. and therefore etc. Yerushalmi chapter 5 of Yevamos: and one does not swim — R' Yaakov in the name of R' Zavdi: this teaches that it is forbidden to float something to convey it from himself; and likewise it is forbidden for a person to float something and bring it to himself — R' Abba Mari and R' Matanya were sitting and saw a certain man spreading water here and there and drinking; R' Abba Mari said to R' Matanya: this is what R' Yochanan bar Zavdi said — it is forbidden for a person to float something and convey it from himself:",
    "7:_": "Seif 7 boat if etc. and if it is. Shabbos 139b: he goes and sleeps etc.; and it must be in such a case; and see in Eruvin 42b regarding leaping and there it implies he deals with floating — it must be when tied; and all the more so in the first case when it does not float at all:"
